---
import PolicyPage from '../components/PolicyPage.astro';

const sections = [
  { href: '#scope', label: 'Scope and responsibility' },
  { href: '#information', label: 'Information we receive' },
  { href: '#use', label: 'How information is used' },
  { href: '#sharing', label: 'Sharing and service providers' },
  { href: '#retention', label: 'Retention and security' },
  { href: '#rights', label: 'Your privacy rights' },
  { href: '#external', label: 'External services and links' },
  { href: '#changes', label: 'Changes to this notice' },
];
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy Notice | The Church of God Nigeria"
  description="How The Church of God Nigeria handles information submitted through tcog.org.ng."
  eyebrow="Website privacy"
  heroTitle="Your trust matters to us."
  heroCopy="This notice explains what information the Nigeria website receives, why it is used, and the choices available to you."
  updated="18 September 2026"
  sections={sections}
  showInternationalPolicy
>
  <section id="scope">
    <h2>Scope and responsibility</h2>
    <p>This notice applies to the website operated for The Church of God Nigeria. The national office is responsible for information submitted through this website and can be contacted at <a href="mailto:Info@tcog.org.ng">Info@tcog.org.ng</a>.</p>
    <p>We aim to handle personal information lawfully, fairly, transparently, and only for clear ministry or administrative purposes, in keeping with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and other applicable requirements.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="information">
    <h2>Information we receive</h2>
    <h3>Information you choose to provide</h3>
    <p>The prayer request form asks for your name, email address, prayer request, and consent. You may also provide a phone number and state or location. If you contact us by email or telephone, we receive the details and message you choose to share.</p>
    <h3>Basic technical information</h3>
    <p>Our hosting and security providers may process routine technical information such as an IP address, browser type, requested page, and time of access to deliver, protect, and troubleshoot the website. We do not currently use an advertising tracker or sell visitor data.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="use">
    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <p>We use information only as reasonably needed to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>receive and respond to prayer requests, enquiries, and requests for church information;</li>
      <li>provide directions or connect a visitor with an appropriate church contact;</li>
      <li>protect the website and diagnose technical problems;</li>
      <li>meet applicable legal, safeguarding, or administrative obligations; and</li>
      <li>maintain records where this is necessary for the purpose for which the information was provided.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Prayer requests are treated with care. Please share only information you are comfortable sending electronically and avoid including another person’s sensitive information without their permission.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <h2>Sharing and service providers</h2>
    <p>We do not rent or sell personal information. Information may be available to authorised national church personnel who need it for the stated purpose. We may also use service providers that support website hosting, form delivery, email, content management, and security.</p>
    <p>The prayer form is delivered through FormSubmit to the national office email account. Those providers process the submission as part of transmitting it. Information may also be disclosed where required by law, or where reasonably necessary to protect a person, the Church, or the public.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2>Retention and security</h2>
    <p>We aim to keep personal information only for as long as it is needed for the purpose for which it was collected, legitimate church administration, safeguarding, or a legal requirement. Retention can vary according to the nature of the communication.</p>
    <p>We take reasonable organisational and technical steps to protect information. However, no email, website, or internet transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="rights">
    <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
    <p>Subject to applicable law, you may ask whether we hold personal information about you and request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or objection to certain processing. You may withdraw consent where consent is the basis for processing.</p>
    <p>Send a request to <a href="mailto:Info@tcog.org.ng?subject=Privacy%20request">Info@tcog.org.ng</a>. We may need enough information to confirm your identity and locate the relevant record. You may also contact the <a href="https://ndpc.gov.ng/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Nigeria Data Protection Commission</a> if you believe your data protection rights have not been respected.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="external">
    <h2>External services and links</h2>
    <p>The website links to or embeds services operated by others, including Google Maps, YouTube, YouTube Music, Spotify, FormSubmit, Vercel, Sanity, and the International Offices website. When you use an external service, its own privacy notice and terms apply. We encourage you to review them before providing information.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
    <p>We may update this notice as the website, our practices, or legal requirements change. The date at the top of this page shows the latest revision. Significant changes will be communicated on the website where appropriate.</p>
  </section>
</PolicyPage>
